# Frontend UX Rules

## Simple vs Expert Mode

`uiStore.uiMode` (`'simple' | 'expert'`, persisted, default `simple`). Switch only through
`sceneWorkflowStore.switchUIMode(mode, focusUsageIndex?)` — it points the expert sidebar at the
running / selected scene before `Sidebar` mounts. Toggle: Settings › Display › Interface
(`AdvancedSettingsSection`).

| Area | Expert | Simple |
| ---- | ------ | ------ |
| Left | `Sidebar` (wizard) | `components/simple/SimpleSoundscapes` — one bubble per scene (usage card) |
| Right | `RightSidebar` chrome | same `RightSidebar`, `AcousticsSection`/`ListenersSection` with `presentation="bubbles"` |

Rules:
1. **Never remount `AcousticsSection` on a mode switch** — it owns simulation poll intervals and the
   IR → `audioRenderingMode` effect. `RightSidebar` keeps an identical element tree in both modes;
   only conditional slots (`{!bubbles && …}`) and styles change. Keep it that way.
2. In Simple mode the left `Sidebar` is unmounted, so `SimpleSoundscapes` owns
   `activeSoundParentIndex` / `isInSoundsStep` (auto-selects a generated scene).
3. The scene pipeline lives in `sceneWorkflowStore` and only **sequences existing store actions**
   (`handleAnalyze`, `handleScenarioAnalyze`, page's `handleSendAnalysisToGeneration`,
   `handleGenerateFiltered`). Add pipeline behaviour to those actions, not to the workflow store.
   Steps are idempotent (skip when the card already has the result) — that is what makes Resume work.
4. One run at a time (analysisStore is single-run); further prompts queue.
5. Expert Sidebar follows a running pipeline via `uiStore.sidebarNavCommand` (seq-based, not persisted).
6. Scene panel body = the real `SoundGenerationSection`; build its props with
   `buildSoundGenerationSectionProps` (`components/layout/sidebar/soundSectionProps.ts`), shared
   with `Sidebar`.
7. **Circle clicks:** an inactive circle → activate only (select the scene for the DAW, enable the
   auralization, go to the listener); the active circle → open / reduce its card. Unfinished scenes
   open their workflow view. Acoustics / listener cards float directly (no wrapper panel) with a `−`
   in the Card header (`Card.onReduce`). Simulation cards switch their auralization off / on with the
   header power button (`Card.onTogglePower`, both modes); listeners stop via the ⋮ menu, and an
   active single listener with its card reduced shows a warning `BubbleExitButton` ("Leave FPS view").
8. **Circle states** (`components/ui/Bubble.tsx`, all circles): pending = frosted + muted icon;
   `ready` = primary border + icon; `ready` + `selected` = solid primary, inverted icon.
   Listener circles use `tone="listener"` (the listener card's warning color, headphones icon).
9. **Headings** ("Soundscapes", "Acoustics", "Listeners") use a difference
   blend. They must be standalone fixed elements (`BubbleHeading`) — never inside a stacking
   context (a fixed/z-indexed parent blends them against nothing). That is why `RightSidebar`'s
   `<aside>` is `display: contents` in bubble mode.
10. Panels reduce on a plain click on the 3D scene (`useDismissOnSceneClick`) — not on drags, UI
    clicks, active viewer modes, or clicks that selected something.
11. Mode switch → Expert expands the left sidebar on the selected scene's Sounds step; → Simple
    reopens the panel of the scene the expert sidebar showed (`pendingSimpleFocus`).

## Scene Bottom Bar

`components/scene/SceneBottomBar.tsx` — full-width frosted strip (`--scene-bottom-bar-height`,
`SCENE_BOTTOM_BAR`) holding every scene-level control: left = "Sound is blue" home (always shown),
a "Simple" button (Expert mode only), undo/redo, save; center = playback (the only transport — the DAW's top status strip has none; the
DAW panel opens above the bar); right = volume, reset
view, refresh, Object Explorer / load model, then shortcuts, notifications, settings. Sidebars stop at
its top edge. Add new scene-level controls here as `BarButton`s — do not reintroduce floating corner
buttons.

## Home Stage (no model)

Every fresh load of `/` starts **empty** (no seeded cards or sounds) on a small fixed grid
(`HOME_STAGE`: 6 × 6 m, 0.5 m cells, nothing drawn on it). `HomeUploadPrompt` ("Upload a 3D model
or start below" — "Upload" opens the load-model dialog via `uiStore.showLoadModelPanel`) sits above
the centred new-scene panel that `SimpleSoundscapes` opens once per page load; in Expert mode the
prompt shows alone above the bottom bar. Opening / uploading a model while Home holds work shows
`ImportSandboxModal`: import into the model, save as a Homepage project then open, discard, or cancel.

## Sidebar 3-Step Wizard

**Flow:** Context (step 0) → Usage (step 1) → Sounds (step 2)

Implemented in `frontend/src/components/layout/Sidebar.tsx`.

### Step Definitions

| Step | Section component | Valid card types | Prerequisite |
| ---- | ----------------- | ---------------- | ------------ |
| 0 — Context | `ContextSection` | `model-analysis`, `audio`, `freeform` | — |
| 1 — Usage | `UsageSection` | `scenario`, `text`, `freeform` | `parentContextOriginalIndex` set |
| 2 — Sounds | `SoundGenerationSection` | sound configs | `parentUsageOriginalIndex` set |

### Key State (Sidebar.tsx)

| Variable | Type | Purpose |
| -------- | ---- | ------- |
| `currentStep` | `0 \| 1 \| 2` | Active wizard step |
| `activeContextOriginalIndex` | `number \| null` | Which context card is active / expanded |
| `activeUsageOriginalIndex` | `number \| null` | Which usage card is active |
| `bypassedUsage` | `boolean` | User skipped the usage step entirely |

### UIStore Fields

| Field | Purpose |
| ----- | ------- |
| `activeSoundParentIndex` | `null` = skip flow, show all sounds regardless of step |
| `isInSoundsStep` | Gates `unifiedSoundscapeData` — sounds must not render before this is `true` |

## Card Linkage System

Cards use **original index fields** that never change even when cards are reordered:

- `parentContextOriginalIndex` — links a usage card to its parent context card
- `parentUsageOriginalIndex` — links a sound to its parent usage card

Usage cards are filtered in step 1 by `activeContextOriginalIndex`.
Sound cards are filtered in step 2 by `activeUsageOriginalIndex`.

### Negative Index Namespace

Audio-type context cards (type `audio`) use:
```
parentUsageOriginalIndex = -(N + 1)
```
where `N` is the context card's original index. This distinguishes audio context linkage from
normal usage linkage (which uses non-negative integers).

## Freeform (Bypass) Cards

| Trigger | Card type | Effect |
| ------- | --------- | ------ |
| "Skip context" | `freeform` context | No `parentContextOriginalIndex`; auto-advances to step 1 on creation |
| "Skip usage" | `freeform` usage | Has `parentContextOriginalIndex`; auto-advances to step 2 on creation |

Default names: `"Untitled context"` / `"Untitled usage"` — editable inline via `display_name`.

## Navigation Guard Pattern

`prevContextLength` and `prevUsageLength` are `useRef` values initialised to the **current card
count at component mount**:

```typescript
const prevContextLength = useRef(contextCards.length)   // init to current count
```

This prevents re-triggering auto-advance when a section remounts during back-navigation.

**Do not convert these refs to state.** They must be non-reactive to work correctly — reactive
state would re-run the effect and falsely trigger navigation.

## FAB Navigation Rules

- Context FAB → advances to Usage (or directly to Sounds for `audio`/`freeform` context cards)
- Usage FAB → advances to Sounds
- FABs are hidden when the target step has no valid destination card

## Breadcrumb Tooltips

| Breadcrumb | Shows |
| ---------- | ----- |
| Context | All context card `display_name` + `(pending)` if not yet analysed |
| Usage | All usage card `display_name` + `(pending)` if no result/foley |
| Sounds | Grouped by usage parent; each sound name + `(pending)` if not in `generatedSounds` |

## Card Expand / Reduce

Expanded card view shows linked child cards and sounds as a placeholder list.
Expand state is **local component state** — do not persist it in any Zustand store.

## Before / After Generation States

Components should render differently based on whether a sound has been generated:

| State | Condition | UI |
| ----- | --------- | -- |
| Before generation | Sound ID not in `generatedSounds` (soundscapeStore) | Generation button + pending badge |
| After generation | Sound ID in `generatedSounds` | WaveSurfer waveform player + re-generate option |

`isInSoundsStep` (uiStore) must be `true` before rendering any generated sound content.

## page.tsx — Intentionally Large

`frontend/src/app/page.tsx` imports 17+ stores and wires all global effects and callbacks.
This is the **orchestration layer** by design — it owns the single-mount lifecycle contract for
the entire app.

Do not decompose store subscriptions into child components to "clean it up". Distributing them
would scatter ownership, break mount ordering, and make global side effects unpredictable.
